{"id": 17, "ts": 1780425053.6174924, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s support for Candidate\u202fC based on his rapid, correct decision\u2011making and calmness in a crisis, and I note Emily\u2019s endorsement of Candidate\u202fB for his strong conscientiousness and stress resilience. However, the crew\u2011cooperation and communication concerns for both candidates are decisive. Candidate\u202fC, while technically excellent, \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d which raises serious doubts about his ability to maintain a collaborative cockpit environment on long\u2011haul flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB, although he \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues,\u201d is \u201cvery conscientious\u201d and \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d indicating high operational reliability and resilience\u2014core safety attributes. Moreover, his \u201cgood at assessing weather conditions\u201d and \u201cexcellent computer skills\u201d directly support the technical demands of international routes. Given that reliability and stress handling are non\u2011negotiable for this role, I am inclined to recommend Candidate\u202fB, provided we address his interpersonal style through targeted training."}
